<p><b data-imt-p=3D"1">Since patch <a href=3D"https://wiki.leagueoflegends.=
com/en-us/V5.13" title=3D"V5.13">V5.13</a>, units can only be affected by t=
he highest slow value during its effect. Any applied slows that have a lowe=
r potency do not further affect the slow amount.</b>
</p><p data-imt-p=3D"1">Prior to patch <a href=3D"https://wiki.leagueoflege=
nds.com/en-us/V5.13" title=3D"V5.13">V5.13</a> slow stacked:
</p><p data-imt-p=3D"1">Slowing effects followed particular rules when stac=
king:
</p>
<ul><li data-imt-p=3D"1">If a champion was affected by multiple slows, the =
strongest one would be fully applied, while the others were applied sequent=
ially with <b>65% reduced effectiveness</b> down to 35% of its original str=
ength.</li></ul>
<ul><li data-imt-p=3D"1">Slow effects derived from items with the same name=
 or <a href=3D"https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Named_item_effect" ti=
tle=3D"Named item effect">named item effect</a> did <b>NOT</b> stack, even =
when coming from different champions. Only the strongest item slow was appl=
ied at any moment. The exception to this was the active effect of <span cla=
ss=3D"inline-image item-icon label-after item-icon tooltips-init-complete" =
style=3D"display:inline;white-space:pre;" data-param=3D"" data-item=3D"Rand=
